1
00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:02,660
Wealth, fame, power.

2
00:00:03,040 --> 00:00:04,577
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

3
00:00:04,660 --> 00:00:07,197
attained this and everything
else the world had to offer,

4
00:00:07,280 --> 00:00:10,456
and his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

5
00:00:10,740 --> 00:00:11,975
You want my treasure?

6
00:00:12,220 --> 00:00:13,420
You can have it.

7
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:16,600
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

8
00:00:16,900 --> 00:00:19,060
Now you just have to find it.

9
00:00:20,940 --> 00:00:24,237
These words lured men to
the Grand Line in pursuit

10
00:00:24,320 --> 00:00:26,757
of dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine.

11
00:00:26,840 --> 00:00:29,517
This is the time known
as the Great Pirate Era.

12
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:35,140
Come aboard and bring along
all your hopes and dreams.

13
00:00:35,700 --> 00:00:40,440
Together we will find everything
that we're looking for.

14
00:00:41,520 --> 00:00:42,700
One piece.

15
00:00:47,440 --> 00:00:52,577
Compass left behind,
it'll only slow us down.

16
00:00:52,660 --> 00:00:58,457
Your heart will be your guide,
raise the sails and take the helm.

17
00:00:58,540 --> 00:01:01,137
That legendary place.

18
00:01:01,220 --> 00:01:03,897
That the end of the map reveals.

19
00:01:03,980 --> 00:01:06,657
Is only legendary.

20
00:01:06,740 --> 00:01:10,117
Until someone proves it real.

21
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:12,557
Through it all.

22
00:01:12,640 --> 00:01:14,497
Through all the trouble and times.

23
00:01:14,580 --> 00:01:16,817
Through the heartache
and through the pain.

24
00:01:16,900 --> 00:01:21,380
Know that I will be there to stand by you.

25
00:01:21,900 --> 00:01:24,240
So I can know you'll stand by me.

26
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:30,477
So come aboard and bring along
all your hopes and dreams.

27
00:01:30,560 --> 00:01:35,897
Together we will find everything
that we're looking for.

28
00:01:35,980 --> 00:01:42,357
There's always room for you
if you want to be my friend.

29
00:01:42,440 --> 00:01:44,637
We are.

30
00:01:44,720 --> 00:01:46,757
We are on the cruise.

31
00:01:46,840 --> 00:01:50,797
We are those three.

32
00:01:50,880 --> 00:01:52,057
Think they can mock me?

33
00:01:52,140 --> 00:01:53,277
Screw that.

34
00:01:53,360 --> 00:01:57,320
I consider this act of
aggression a declaration of war.

35
00:01:59,120 --> 00:02:00,980
There you are, Mohji.

36
00:02:02,340 --> 00:02:06,360
I hope you wouldn't mind if I
take the pirate hunter's head.

37
00:02:06,680 --> 00:02:08,320
Be my guest.

38
00:02:26,160 --> 00:02:27,395
What's with this dog?

39
00:02:29,100 --> 00:02:29,930
Doggy!

40
00:02:36,440 --> 00:02:38,734
Zoro, it looks like this dog is frozen.

41
00:02:38,860 --> 00:02:42,566
I don't give a damn, he could
sit there forever for all I care.

42
00:02:42,860 --> 00:02:44,280
I wonder if it's dead.

43
00:02:58,240 --> 00:03:01,240
Luffy, please, quit goofing
around and get serious.

44
00:03:04,080 --> 00:03:05,000
Damn dog.

45
00:03:05,460 --> 00:03:06,860
I don't feel good.

46
00:03:11,260 --> 00:03:13,160
Oh, hi, Navigator.

47
00:03:13,520 --> 00:03:15,049
I guess you can have this.

48
00:03:15,200 --> 00:03:17,788
You got me out of a
pretty sticky situation.

49
00:03:19,020 --> 00:03:20,820
Great, the key to the cage.

50
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:22,297
Did you go steal it for me?

51
00:03:22,380 --> 00:03:23,420
Thanks, Nami.

52
00:03:23,880 --> 00:03:25,821
They only did it so we'd be even.

53
00:03:27,440 --> 00:03:28,270
Yeah, sure.

54
00:03:42,340 --> 00:03:44,120
Stupid, stupid, stupid dog!

55
00:03:51,080 --> 00:03:52,540
Hey, stop that?

56
00:03:53,520 --> 00:03:55,317
Stop picking on poor Chouchou!

57
00:03:55,400 --> 00:03:56,341
Leave him alone.

58
00:03:58,640 --> 00:04:00,360
Who might you be, old man?

59
00:04:00,560 --> 00:04:05,501
Old man, why, I'm the mayor of this town Who
are you and why are you hurting Chouchou?

60
00:04:13,740 --> 00:04:14,580
How's Zoro?

61
00:04:14,960 --> 00:04:16,997
I told him he really should see a doctor.

62
00:04:17,080 --> 00:04:19,017
But he insisted that he didn't need to!

63
00:04:19,100 --> 00:04:20,982
and just wanted to sleep it off.

64
00:04:22,920 --> 00:04:25,240
So this dog's name is Chouchou?

65
00:04:26,660 --> 00:04:28,617
Why is he just sitting there like that?

66
00:04:28,700 --> 00:04:30,100
He sure is a lazy dog.

67
00:04:30,320 --> 00:04:31,740
He's guarding the store.

68
00:04:32,380 --> 00:04:33,210
Huh?

69
00:04:34,080 --> 00:04:35,357
Oh, I see.

70
00:04:35,440 --> 00:04:36,675
It's a pet food shop.

71
00:04:37,020 --> 00:04:37,860
That's right.

72
00:04:38,120 --> 00:04:42,296
And the man who used to run this
store was a very close friend of mine.

73
00:04:46,580 --> 00:04:47,760
There you go.

74
00:04:50,080 --> 00:04:54,540
When he passed, I assume the
responsibility of taking care of Chouchou.

75
00:04:55,720 --> 00:04:56,720
He died?

76
00:04:57,560 --> 00:04:58,390
Yes.

77
00:04:58,473 --> 00:05:02,440
Three months ago, after fighting
his illness for a very long time.

78
00:05:03,160 --> 00:05:07,336
Don't tell me he's been waiting for
his master to return all this time.

79
00:05:07,960 --> 00:05:09,940
That seems to be the consensus.

80
00:05:13,120 --> 00:05:13,950
Huh.

81
00:05:17,560 --> 00:05:20,240
But I find that very hard to believe.

82
00:05:22,060 --> 00:05:23,760
Chouchou is a smart dog.

83
00:05:24,680 --> 00:05:28,562
He's probably known for a while
that his master isn't coming back.

84
00:05:32,240 --> 00:05:34,800
Then why does he stay here at the store?

85
00:05:35,060 --> 00:05:37,017
I guess because he has a connection to it.

86
00:05:37,100 --> 00:05:38,697
It's his treasure.

87
00:05:38,780 --> 00:05:40,240
He's guarding it.

88
00:05:41,780 --> 00:05:45,657
His master left him with this shop,
and that's why he protects it.

89
00:05:45,740 --> 00:05:48,917
I've tried to bring him back to my place
so he won't be out in the elements,

90
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:52,000
but he won't take so much
as a step away from here.

91
00:06:08,140 --> 00:06:09,037
What's that sound?

92
00:06:09,120 --> 00:06:09,950
It's him!

93
00:06:10,033 --> 00:06:10,863
Beast Tamer-Moji!

94
00:06:10,946 --> 00:06:11,960
We gotta go! Run!

95
00:06:13,300 --> 00:06:15,260
What do you mean by Beast Tamer?

96
00:06:15,460 --> 00:06:16,960
Wait, hold on!

97
00:06:17,860 --> 00:06:19,797
Come on, puppy, something's here.

98
00:06:19,880 --> 00:06:22,292
Why don't you just give me that key back?

99
00:06:26,500 --> 00:06:30,740
I see that your friends have deserted
you, and after you just escaped.

100
00:06:31,620 --> 00:06:33,000
Who the heck are you?

101
00:06:33,200 --> 00:06:37,320
I'm known as the Beast Tamer-Moji,
a member of the Buggy Pirates.

102
00:06:37,860 --> 00:06:40,820
Whoa, that's a weird
animal suit you got on.

103
00:06:41,060 --> 00:06:42,180
That was rude.

104
00:06:42,480 --> 00:06:43,900
This is manly hair.

105
00:06:44,180 --> 00:06:45,709
Okay, that's even weirder.

106
00:06:45,880 --> 00:06:49,657
You shouldn't assume that you're safe
just because you're in that cage.

107
00:06:49,740 --> 00:06:52,152
You must not know of my terrifying skill.

108
00:06:52,360 --> 00:06:57,301
There is no animal in this world that Beast
Tame Emoji can't bend to do his bidding.

109
00:06:58,340 --> 00:06:59,170
Shake.

110
00:07:01,520 --> 00:07:03,100
Why does it hurt so bad?

111
00:07:03,360 --> 00:07:05,737
You nameless thief, I've
no interest in killing you,

112
00:07:05,820 --> 00:07:10,100
but tell me where Roronoa Zoro
is before I change my mind.

113
00:07:10,320 --> 00:07:11,220
No way!

114
00:07:11,640 --> 00:07:13,240
Ritchie, attack!

115
00:07:17,600 --> 00:07:19,380
Yes, I'm finally out!

116
00:07:24,660 --> 00:07:25,800
Nice work.

117
00:07:26,260 --> 00:07:27,780
Good boy, Ritchie.

118
00:07:27,980 --> 00:07:32,274
Now let's go find Zoro so I can defeat
him and strengthen my reputation.

119
00:07:33,300 --> 00:07:34,317
What's wrong?

120
00:07:34,400 --> 00:07:36,280
Oh, it's a pet food store.

121
00:07:36,520 --> 00:07:37,657
Make it quick, then.

122
00:07:37,740 --> 00:07:38,570
Let's go.

123
00:07:42,120 --> 00:07:47,040
Don't tell me this pathetic little thing
really thinks he can guard the shop.

124
00:07:51,600 --> 00:07:52,860
That was intense.

125
00:07:53,320 --> 00:07:55,320
At least now I'm out of that cage.

126
00:07:58,240 --> 00:08:01,017
First thing, I teach those
buggy pirates a lesson,

127
00:08:01,100 --> 00:08:04,317
and then I convince Nami to
be the navigator for my crew.

128
00:08:04,400 --> 00:08:05,230
Huh?

129
00:08:05,313 --> 00:08:06,597
How did you survive that attack?

130
00:08:06,680 --> 00:08:07,540
You're alive?

131
00:08:07,820 --> 00:08:09,420
I just got lucky, I guess.

132
00:08:09,780 --> 00:08:11,997
Surviving an attack
like that isn't normal.

133
00:08:12,080 --> 00:08:13,997
I figured you'd be scattered all over.

134
00:08:14,080 --> 00:08:15,140
It's not normal.

135
00:08:15,800 --> 00:08:18,617
Why exactly did you decide
to come to this town?

136
00:08:18,700 --> 00:08:20,737
And how'd you get involved
with those pirates?

137
00:08:20,820 --> 00:08:23,117
All I'm doing is searching
for a chart of the Grand

138
00:08:23,200 --> 00:08:26,082
Line and a good navigator
to join my pirate crew.

139
00:08:28,480 --> 00:08:33,245
I think that guy in the animal suit said
he was looking for Zoro, so I gotta go.

140
00:08:44,480 --> 00:08:47,680
Chouchou, this shop belongs
to the two of us now.

141
00:08:54,100 --> 00:08:56,740
That bag is way too big for you, Chouchou.

142
00:09:09,380 --> 00:09:12,497
Ha-ha-ha-ha-ha...

143
00:09:12,580 --> 00:09:14,080
Be careful, Chouchou.

144
00:09:14,240 --> 00:09:15,416
Don't hurt yourself.

145
00:09:15,560 --> 00:09:16,580
Leave this to me.

146
00:09:19,260 --> 00:09:22,201
Pat Chouchou, I told you
not to eat the merchandise.

147
00:09:22,580 --> 00:09:24,160
Now let's chow down!

148
00:09:35,700 --> 00:09:38,020
Well, not ready to give up yet.

149
00:09:40,420 --> 00:09:42,820
Chouchou, I'm getting on in years now.

150
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:45,077
I gotta go see the doctor for a checkup.

151
00:09:45,160 --> 00:09:48,320
But I'll be back, so guard
the shop until I return.

152
00:09:48,800 --> 00:09:50,940
I'm counting on you, Chouchou.

153
00:09:52,560 --> 00:09:54,000
Hold down the fort.

154
00:10:30,600 --> 00:10:33,040
He has a connection to it.

155
00:10:33,300 --> 00:10:34,317
It's his treasure.

156
00:10:34,400 --> 00:10:36,060
He's guarding it.

157
00:10:36,280 --> 00:10:40,104
His master left him with this shop
and that's why he protects it.

158
00:11:04,960 --> 00:11:08,254
Dammit, I can't believe that
annoying little dog bit me.

159
00:11:15,640 --> 00:11:17,560
Wait, I thought I killed you.

160
00:11:17,700 --> 00:11:19,524
What are you still doing alive?

161
00:11:20,860 --> 00:11:23,680
I'm afraid you can't get
rid of me that easily.

162
00:11:24,060 --> 00:11:26,884
This time, Crush's head
into the ground, Richie!

163
00:11:30,660 --> 00:11:32,980
I'm not gonna be beaten by a lion!

164
00:11:34,400 --> 00:11:35,230
Gum-Gum!

165
00:11:38,900 --> 00:11:39,730
Hammer!

166
00:11:49,620 --> 00:11:51,020
What are you?

167
00:11:53,280 --> 00:11:57,120
Well, I ate the Gum-Gum Devil Fruit.

168
00:11:57,400 --> 00:12:02,640
So then you have Devil Fruit powers like
Captain Buggy, but yours make you rubber?

169
00:12:07,260 --> 00:12:08,090
Sorry!

170
00:12:08,173 --> 00:12:09,649
I apologize for attacking!

171
00:12:09,780 --> 00:12:11,251
I don't want any trouble!

172
00:12:11,480 --> 00:12:14,057
There's no reason for
you to apologize to me.

173
00:12:14,140 --> 00:12:17,552
Because of you, that dog will
never get his treasure back.

174
00:12:19,760 --> 00:12:23,760
And now, because of that,
I'm going to kick your ass.

175
00:12:45,200 --> 00:12:46,577
Pirates are all the same.

176
00:12:46,660 --> 00:12:49,425
They're all just a bunch
of heartless bastards.

177
00:12:49,740 --> 00:12:54,077
They destroy everything that people hold
dear without giving it a second thought.

178
00:12:54,160 --> 00:12:56,780
Oh, you're alive, pirate! You know,

179
00:12:56,960 --> 00:13:00,657
I thought for sure that lion was going
to tear your head off and end it all.

180
00:13:00,740 --> 00:13:04,357
And I wish he had, because then there'd
be one less pirate in the world!

181
00:13:04,440 --> 00:13:06,337
Maybe I should kill you
right now before you

182
00:13:06,420 --> 00:13:09,220
can gather a crew and
destroy everything else!

183
00:13:10,360 --> 00:13:11,190
Come now.

184
00:13:11,273 --> 00:13:12,237
There's no need for violence.

185
00:13:12,320 --> 00:13:13,797
As if you could ever kill me.

186
00:13:13,880 --> 00:13:15,762
Well, maybe I'll try it and see!

187
00:13:16,080 --> 00:13:16,910
I said stop!

188
00:13:16,993 --> 00:13:17,993
What's with you people?

189
00:13:31,660 --> 00:13:33,537
Sorry, but that's all I could say for you.

190
00:13:33,620 --> 00:13:36,120
That bastard lion ate all the rest of it.

191
00:13:37,860 --> 00:13:38,690
He...

192
00:13:38,773 --> 00:13:42,340
he fought the lion in order
to save the dog's food?

193
00:13:46,260 --> 00:13:47,480
You fought well.

194
00:13:47,880 --> 00:13:50,357
Of course, I didn't actually
see you defend the store,

195
00:13:50,440 --> 00:13:52,558
but I can tell you gave it your all.

196
00:14:10,300 --> 00:14:11,180
Thanks!

197
00:14:11,480 --> 00:14:13,440
Good luck to you, too, doggy!

198
00:14:27,840 --> 00:14:30,640
You were defeated? How?

199
00:14:31,440 --> 00:14:33,120
I'm very sorry, Captain.

200
00:14:33,340 --> 00:14:34,740
Sorry, I failed.

201
00:14:35,520 --> 00:14:38,600
Moji, I can't believe you
were defeated by Zoro.

202
00:14:38,900 --> 00:14:40,160
No, it wasn't Zoro.

203
00:14:40,300 --> 00:14:41,497
It was that Straw Hat.

204
00:14:41,580 --> 00:14:42,410
What?

205
00:14:42,493 --> 00:14:45,497
There's no way that skinny little punk
could have gotten the better of you.

206
00:14:45,580 --> 00:14:46,920
He's eating the gum.

207
00:14:47,480 --> 00:14:49,320
Now I'm really pissed off.

208
00:14:49,660 --> 00:14:52,377
All right, prepare all the
remaining special buggy balls.

209
00:14:52,460 --> 00:14:55,813
I'm gonna blow this entire
miserable town to smithereens.

210
00:14:57,500 --> 00:15:01,057
Sorry about earlier I
didn't mean to yell at

211
00:15:01,140 --> 00:15:04,417
you that's okay you've
been under a lot of stress

212
00:15:04,500 --> 00:15:10,737
lately but hey no need
to apologize I'm pathetic

213
00:15:10,820 --> 00:15:13,477
shu shu and this young one
have fought so hard and

214
00:15:13,560 --> 00:15:15,897
yet I the mayor have
done nothing but sit back

215
00:15:15,980 --> 00:15:18,757
and watch our town be
obliterated by buggy and his

216
00:15:18,840 --> 00:15:22,057
despicable crew calm
down it's not that bad 40

217
00:15:22,140 --> 00:15:25,960
years ago this whole area was
nothing but Barren, rugged land.

218
00:15:26,160 --> 00:15:29,300
We all work together to
create fields for our crops.

219
00:15:29,540 --> 00:15:32,893
We opened stores and built
everything from the ground up.

220
00:15:33,020 --> 00:15:35,817
This town is a treasure to
me and all its citizens.

221
00:15:35,900 --> 00:15:40,540
From here on out, I refuse to let Buggy
and his crew terrorize us anymore!

222
00:15:41,180 --> 00:15:42,940
Fire a special, Buggy Ball.

223
00:15:43,240 --> 00:15:44,620
Blow this town away!

224
00:15:56,460 --> 00:15:58,240
He'll destroy it all.

225
00:15:59,680 --> 00:16:01,380
Zoro was sleeping in there!

226
00:16:01,800 --> 00:16:03,740
I'm sure he's dead now.

227
00:16:06,140 --> 00:16:07,400
Zoro, you in there?

228
00:16:07,560 --> 00:16:08,617
Are you still alive?

229
00:16:08,700 --> 00:16:11,171
That's one hell of a way to wake a guy up.

230
00:16:14,540 --> 00:16:16,800
I could have used a few more Zs.

231
00:16:17,960 --> 00:16:20,020
How did you survive that blast?

232
00:16:20,540 --> 00:16:22,257
Oh, right! You're alive!

233
00:16:22,340 --> 00:16:25,020
I refuse to let him get away with this.

234
00:16:26,060 --> 00:16:27,800
I won't stand for it.

235
00:16:27,980 --> 00:16:30,837
I can't let this scumbag destroy all of my

236
00:16:30,920 --> 00:16:33,449
townspeople worked for
these last 40 years.

237
00:16:35,200 --> 00:16:37,920
I am the mayor of this town.

238
00:16:39,100 --> 00:16:41,640
I will protect it and its inhabitants.

239
00:16:41,980 --> 00:16:45,580
I swear to my dying breath. Stop!

240
00:16:45,760 --> 00:16:47,037
You can't defeat Buggy!

241
00:16:47,120 --> 00:16:50,457
Perhaps, but there are some
fights that a man can't run from.

242
00:16:50,540 --> 00:16:51,540
Isn't that right?

243
00:16:51,940 --> 00:16:53,234
That's right, old man.

244
00:16:53,760 --> 00:16:54,780
Shut up!

245
00:16:55,040 --> 00:16:56,137
Don't egg him on, Luffy.

246
00:16:56,220 --> 00:16:58,177
It's dangerous for him to fight Back.

247
00:16:58,260 --> 00:17:00,060
I know it's dangerous!

248
00:17:02,880 --> 00:17:06,780
I'm coming for you, Back the Clown!

249
00:17:07,600 --> 00:17:10,980
The mayor was crying. He was?

250
00:17:11,420 --> 00:17:12,640
I didn't notice.

251
00:17:12,920 --> 00:17:15,567
Looks like the party's
getting more exciting.

252
00:17:15,740 --> 00:17:16,760
Sure does.

253
00:17:17,880 --> 00:17:19,760
This is no time for laughter.

254
00:17:20,580 --> 00:17:23,639
Don't worry, I started to
grow fond of that old man.

255
00:17:23,860 --> 00:17:25,684
There's no way I'd let him die.

256
00:17:25,840 --> 00:17:27,480
Well, in that case...

257
00:17:28,120 --> 00:17:29,296
You're gonna go too?

258
00:17:29,520 --> 00:17:30,402
You're wounded!

259
00:17:30,760 --> 00:17:31,820
Yeah, so what?

260
00:17:31,960 --> 00:17:35,960
The injury to my reputation's a lot
worse than the injury to my gut.

261
00:17:36,140 --> 00:17:41,160
Well, if we want to get to the grand
line, we better go steal that chart back.

262
00:17:42,940 --> 00:17:43,770
Ha!

263
00:17:43,853 --> 00:17:45,377
Are you gonna join our crew or what?

264
00:17:45,460 --> 00:17:46,657
Huh? Come on!

265
00:17:46,740 --> 00:17:49,860
I'll never sink so low
as to become a pirate.

266
00:17:52,740 --> 00:17:56,681
But I suppose we could team up in
order to achieve our common goal?

267
00:17:57,860 --> 00:17:59,317
Second shot is ready sir.

268
00:17:59,400 --> 00:18:00,980
All right, then fire

269
00:18:07,200 --> 00:18:09,717
I'm mayor Battle in
this town is my treasure

270
00:18:09,800 --> 00:18:12,497
I won't let you terrorize
my people any longer.

271
00:18:12,580 --> 00:18:16,600
So come out and fight me you
idiot This town is no treasure.

272
00:18:16,820 --> 00:18:19,017
Treasure is gold, silver, and jewelry.

273
00:18:19,100 --> 00:18:22,217
So cut the crap, old man, and get
out of here before I kill you.

274
00:18:22,300 --> 00:18:24,720
You can never understand how I feel!

275
00:18:26,220 --> 00:18:30,537
Soon I'm going to conquer the Grand Line
and flashily obtain all the world's riches.

276
00:18:30,620 --> 00:18:32,857
And there's nothing you can do to stop me.

277
00:18:32,940 --> 00:18:34,817
All the world would belong to me.

278
00:18:34,900 --> 00:18:36,777
Now, if this town means so much to you,

279
00:18:36,860 --> 00:18:39,297
then perhaps I'll do you a
favor and kill you first.

280
00:18:39,380 --> 00:18:43,145
That way you won't have to see
me destroy your precious village.

281
00:18:43,280 --> 00:18:44,280
Shut up!

282
00:18:44,460 --> 00:18:45,820
And fight me already!

283
00:18:46,160 --> 00:18:47,640
Don't get cocky.

284
00:18:47,920 --> 00:18:52,080
I'll never let you destroy this
town, if it costs me my very life!

285
00:18:53,460 --> 00:18:54,560
So be it.

286
00:18:57,300 --> 00:18:59,040
That Straw Hat's not again!

287
00:19:03,760 --> 00:19:07,466
I'm here to kick your ass, just
like I promised I would, Buggy.

288
00:19:16,180 --> 00:19:17,340
How dare you!

289
00:19:17,720 --> 00:19:20,677
You can't just waltz up to
me and treat me like this!

290
00:19:20,760 --> 00:19:23,520
I'm Captain Buggy and
I won't stand for it!

291
00:19:23,780 --> 00:19:26,577
Listen to me, all I want is
the chart and the treasure,

292
00:19:26,660 --> 00:19:28,277
then I'm out of here, you got it?

293
00:19:28,360 --> 00:19:29,640
Yeah, I got it.

294
00:19:30,820 --> 00:19:32,020
Get out of here.

295
00:19:32,180 --> 00:19:33,440
Why'd you follow me?

296
00:19:33,860 --> 00:19:36,100
You're outsiders, leave this to me!

297
00:19:38,140 --> 00:19:42,300
This is my fight that I need to
be the one to protect my town.

298
00:19:46,020 --> 00:19:47,500
Buggy is my fight!

299
00:19:55,920 --> 00:19:58,117
What the hell do you think you're doing?

300
00:19:58,200 --> 00:19:59,965
Why'd you knock out the mayor?

301
00:20:02,480 --> 00:20:03,310
Because...

302
00:20:03,393 --> 00:20:04,817
That's not a bad idea.

303
00:20:04,900 --> 00:20:08,277
As the old man had continued
to fight, he would have died.

304
00:20:08,360 --> 00:20:09,536
That's for the best.

305
00:20:09,880 --> 00:20:11,417
You didn't have to hit him!

306
00:20:11,500 --> 00:20:16,088
I'm sure I could have thought of a more
humane way to deal with the situation!

307
00:20:25,660 --> 00:20:28,457
That's the worst thing you
could have said to him!

308
00:20:28,540 --> 00:20:31,280
Oh, you damn flashy idiot!

309
00:20:31,820 --> 00:20:33,380
I won't stand for this!

310
00:20:34,220 --> 00:20:36,400
Take aim and fire the Buckyball!

311
00:20:37,780 --> 00:20:39,368
Why'd you have to say that?

312
00:20:39,940 --> 00:20:41,800
Come on, Luffy, we gotta go.

313
00:20:41,940 --> 00:20:42,920
You go ahead.

314
00:20:43,280 --> 00:20:44,300
Time to die!

315
00:20:44,720 --> 00:20:46,800
I'm fine, just watch.

316
00:20:48,240 --> 00:20:49,680
Bum, bum, bum!

317
00:20:55,180 --> 00:20:56,400
What is he?

318
00:20:56,680 --> 00:20:58,268
Did he catch the Buckyball?

319
00:21:00,920 --> 00:21:02,260
Run for us!

320
00:21:02,900 --> 00:21:04,440
He could have warned me.

321
00:21:12,720 --> 00:21:14,420
All right, I got him!

322
00:21:14,560 --> 00:21:16,477
What the hell kind of monster are you?

323
00:21:16,560 --> 00:21:18,207
I think you freaked her out.

324
00:21:26,660 --> 00:21:30,297
I knew that something was weird after
you survived the fight with that lion!

325
00:21:30,380 --> 00:21:33,615
No human being can do what
you do Now explain yourself,

326
00:21:33,780 --> 00:21:37,157
what the hell was the balloon
inflatey thing that you did just now?

327
00:21:37,240 --> 00:21:38,946
That was the Gum-Gum balloon.

328
00:21:39,240 --> 00:21:41,517
I don't care what you call it,
just tell me how you did it!

329
00:21:41,600 --> 00:21:43,541
What are you, some kind of freak?

330
00:21:44,980 --> 00:21:47,960
How dare you try to flashily do me in!

331
00:21:54,360 --> 00:21:56,380
Unreal, using his men as a shield.

332
00:22:03,300 --> 00:22:04,130
Hm?

333
00:22:04,980 --> 00:22:07,160
What in the world just happened here?

334
00:22:08,960 --> 00:22:10,800
No! It's you!

335
00:22:11,900 --> 00:22:14,100
Ah, it's that damn Straw Hat!

336
00:22:14,940 --> 00:22:16,977
Captain Buggy, we have to be careful.

337
00:22:17,060 --> 00:22:18,577
He has Devil Fruit powers too.

338
00:22:18,660 --> 00:22:19,837
He's a rubber person.

339
00:22:19,920 --> 00:22:21,620
I saw it myself. What?

340
00:22:22,360 --> 00:22:24,080
Rubber person? Yeah.

341
00:22:26,040 --> 00:22:27,740
A Devil Fruit.

342
00:22:28,160 --> 00:22:31,454
That explains how he bounced
that buggy ball back to us.

343
00:22:37,400 --> 00:22:40,400
How do you plan to respond
to this insult, Captain?

344
00:22:40,820 --> 00:22:41,980
Oh, Kappa G.

345
00:22:42,660 --> 00:22:43,560
I don't know.

346
00:22:43,700 --> 00:22:45,288
I'm too angry to even fart.

347
00:22:45,520 --> 00:22:46,757
Put him down, Kappa G.

348
00:22:46,840 --> 00:22:48,797
What the hell did you do to my Ritchie?

349
00:22:48,880 --> 00:22:49,710
This cat?

350
00:22:50,160 --> 00:22:53,689
I used it as a shield to keep
my clothes from getting dirty.

351
00:22:55,560 --> 00:22:56,390
Ritchie!

352
00:22:58,540 --> 00:22:59,460
No, Ritchie!

353
00:22:59,580 --> 00:23:00,817
Say something, please!

354
00:23:00,900 --> 00:23:01,730
Ritchie!

355
00:23:06,400 --> 00:23:07,230
Ritchie!

356
00:23:07,313 --> 00:23:08,143
Damn you!

357
00:23:08,240 --> 00:23:09,320
You bastard!

358
00:23:12,040 --> 00:23:13,440
Out of my way!

359
00:23:13,740 --> 00:23:16,200
How about out of my way?

360
00:23:27,120 --> 00:23:31,840
You may call me Acrobat Copper Team,
Captain Buggy's chief of staff.

361
00:23:32,060 --> 00:23:34,260
You will pay for your insolence.

362
00:23:36,500 --> 00:23:38,200
I'll clash swords with you.

363
00:23:39,840 --> 00:23:42,540
It's an honor, Roronoa Zoro.

364
00:23:42,900 --> 00:23:46,900
As a swordsman myself, I
relish this chance to slay you.

365
00:23:49,120 --> 00:23:51,760
Hey, Zoro, you really
should get some rest.

366
00:23:51,880 --> 00:23:52,957
Let me handle this guy.

367
00:23:53,040 --> 00:23:53,980
Just stay back.

368
00:23:55,000 --> 00:23:58,588
That's the stab wound the captain
inflicted on him, the fool.

369
00:23:59,480 --> 00:24:00,680
Harsinus, technique!

370
00:24:02,060 --> 00:24:02,890
Ah!

371
00:24:10,940 --> 00:24:11,860
What's wrong?

372
00:24:12,160 --> 00:24:14,631
I didn't kick you that hard enough, did I?

373
00:24:14,880 --> 00:24:17,920
He fights dirty, going
after his injury like that.

374
00:24:21,100 --> 00:24:22,157
Acrobat technique?

375
00:24:22,240 --> 00:24:24,180
Murder at the steam bath.

376
00:24:26,460 --> 00:24:27,820
Acrobat, my ass.

377
00:24:28,000 --> 00:24:30,059
That's just an ordinary dust cloud.

378
00:24:35,840 --> 00:24:36,920
He did it again!

379
00:24:38,600 --> 00:24:39,440
What's this?

380
00:24:39,840 --> 00:24:43,193
It's such a disgraceful sight
to see a grown man moaning.

381
00:24:43,500 --> 00:24:48,600
I suppose now you can see how foolish it
was to make an enemy of the buggy pirates.

382
00:24:51,220 --> 00:24:55,257
He's hurt so bad, I don't know how
he's managing to stay in the fight.

383
00:24:55,340 --> 00:24:57,397
Why are you just standing
there watching him?

384
00:24:57,480 --> 00:24:59,833
He's gonna get himself killed, you know?

385
00:25:06,760 --> 00:25:09,620
Roranoa's Zoro is finished!

386
00:25:10,500 --> 00:25:12,700
You annoying little bastard.

387
00:25:14,140 --> 00:25:16,760
You having fun poking in my wound?

388
00:25:17,060 --> 00:25:18,500
Then go ahead!

389
00:25:22,360 --> 00:25:23,200
Ouchie!

390
00:25:27,940 --> 00:25:30,300
Why didn't you dodge his attack?

391
00:25:31,120 --> 00:25:33,580
Is that enough of a handicap for you?

392
00:25:35,400 --> 00:25:40,340
And now let me show you just how
superior my skills are to yours

393
00:25:44,420 --> 00:25:47,000
You've made a vast error in judgment.

394
00:25:47,360 --> 00:25:52,580
I won't be mocked my swords aim
to be the world's greatest I

395
00:25:53,420 --> 00:25:57,640
Refuse to lose even once to anyone
who calls himself a swordsman.

396
00:25:58,040 --> 00:25:59,120
I see

397
00:26:00,300 --> 00:26:02,241
A strong resolve keeps you going.

398
00:26:02,660 --> 00:26:04,060
But have no fear.

399
00:26:04,540 --> 00:26:08,128
Wounds as bad as yours will be
more than enough of an excuse.

400
00:26:09,860 --> 00:26:11,580
For losing to me.

401
00:26:12,140 --> 00:26:13,199
To hell with that.

402
00:26:15,140 --> 00:26:19,140
If I lose to someone like you,
even with these minimal injuries,

403
00:26:19,520 --> 00:26:22,873
then I don't have a very bright
future ahead of me, do I?

404
00:26:24,920 --> 00:26:25,957
Why, you...

405
00:26:26,040 --> 00:26:27,680
All right, yeah! Yeah!

406
00:26:29,700 --> 00:26:31,420
I won't stay and watch this.

407
00:26:31,560 --> 00:26:33,577
You pirates can stand around for the rest

408
00:26:33,660 --> 00:26:36,177
of time and kill each
other for all I care.

409
00:26:36,260 --> 00:26:39,848
I mean, it doesn't matter to me
whether you guys win or lose.

410
00:26:40,600 --> 00:26:45,071
I'm gonna take this opportunity to swipe
their treasure and get out of here.

411
00:26:46,300 --> 00:26:49,418
Maybe we can team up again
if we ever get the chance.

412
00:26:49,580 --> 00:26:51,457
See ya, good luck with the fight.

413
00:26:51,540 --> 00:26:53,160
Yeah, thanks, see ya!

414
00:26:53,860 --> 00:26:56,620
Here's a taste of my
ultimate acrobatic move.

415
00:27:00,040 --> 00:27:04,220
Acrobat technique, the dance
of a hundred kamikaze times.

416
00:27:09,460 --> 00:27:12,200
Acrobat technique, a
hike in the mountains.

417
00:27:13,360 --> 00:27:15,800
Fireworks in the cool summer breeze.

418
00:27:16,680 --> 00:27:18,420
Whoa, that's high.

419
00:27:18,700 --> 00:27:20,620
Sting of the unicycle.

420
00:27:22,220 --> 00:27:24,380
Ground hugging, chop chop colonel.

421
00:27:27,700 --> 00:27:29,580
Kamaji, I'll hold him.

422
00:27:29,760 --> 00:27:31,860
Then you finish him off. Duh.

423
00:27:33,660 --> 00:27:34,700
Damn it.

424
00:27:42,040 --> 00:27:42,870
Luffy.

425
00:27:43,740 --> 00:27:45,100
You bastard.

426
00:27:45,820 --> 00:27:49,740
If you want to fight
someone, how about me?

427
00:27:54,400 --> 00:27:58,480
I assure you, I don't need my
captain's help to finish you off.

428
00:27:59,300 --> 00:28:00,130
Enough.

429
00:28:00,213 --> 00:28:01,420
I'm tired of this.

430
00:28:03,900 --> 00:28:06,400
So you've finally given up, have you?

431
00:28:06,980 --> 00:28:08,117
I must say,

432
00:28:08,200 --> 00:28:12,077
I'm quite impressed that you lasted
that long with such serious injuries.

433
00:28:12,160 --> 00:28:13,689
I think you misunderstood.

434
00:28:14,640 --> 00:28:18,400
I'm tired of watching your
boring little sideshow.

435
00:28:19,740 --> 00:28:22,300
So sorry to have disappointed you.

436
00:28:22,600 --> 00:28:26,900
How about my real swordsman skills?

437
00:28:29,500 --> 00:28:30,360
Die, Zoro!

438
00:28:32,420 --> 00:28:33,380
Rain!

439
00:28:33,960 --> 00:28:34,800
Giddy!

440
00:28:39,260 --> 00:28:40,220
Comedy!

441
00:28:42,760 --> 00:28:47,620
I can't believe the Buggy Pirates
were defeated by Betty Thieves.

442
00:28:51,220 --> 00:28:53,200
We aren't petty thieves.

443
00:28:56,660 --> 00:28:58,100
We're pirates.

444
00:29:00,300 --> 00:29:03,400
Luke, I'm going to sleep. Good.

445
00:29:03,720 --> 00:29:05,540
I'm looking forward to this.

446
00:29:11,060 --> 00:29:12,800
You guys are pirates?

447
00:29:13,280 --> 00:29:16,020
Yeah, we're searching for the Grand Line.

448
00:29:17,000 --> 00:29:17,830
Ha!

449
00:29:17,913 --> 00:29:19,617
That's not an easy voyage, you know,

450
00:29:19,700 --> 00:29:22,997
and I don't think that two halfwits
the likes of you can handle it.

451
00:29:23,080 --> 00:29:26,997
And what will you do if by some
miracle you manage to make it there?

452
00:29:27,080 --> 00:29:29,315
Go on a sightseeing tour or something?

453
00:29:33,600 --> 00:29:35,140
Be king of the pirates!

454
00:29:36,960 --> 00:29:38,977
You can't be serious, you idiot!

455
00:29:39,060 --> 00:29:42,257
If you were king of the pirates,
then that would make me God!

456
00:29:42,340 --> 00:29:43,170
God,

457
00:29:43,253 --> 00:29:44,517
there's only one who can be king of the

458
00:29:44,600 --> 00:29:46,677
pirates and obtain all
this world's treasures,

459
00:29:46,760 --> 00:29:48,819
and that's gonna be me, you got it?

460
00:29:49,040 --> 00:29:50,060
You're annoying.

461
00:29:51,200 --> 00:29:53,140
Let's go ahead and settle this.

462
00:29:55,640 --> 00:29:58,257
Seeing that Straw Hat
brings back memories of him,

463
00:29:58,340 --> 00:30:00,277
and that really gets my blood boiling.

464
00:30:00,360 --> 00:30:02,478
So bring it on, you wanted a pirate.

465
00:30:02,640 --> 00:30:04,340
You remind me of him.

466
00:30:04,860 --> 00:30:07,480
That damn cheeky red-haired pirate.

467
00:30:07,980 --> 00:30:09,160
What did you say?

468
00:30:09,420 --> 00:30:10,500
The red hair.

469
00:30:11,160 --> 00:30:14,037
Wait, are you saying you
knew my old friend, Shanks?

470
00:30:14,120 --> 00:30:14,950
That's right.

471
00:30:15,160 --> 00:30:16,720
I knew Shanks once.

472
00:30:16,920 --> 00:30:18,217
Do you know where he is now?

473
00:30:18,300 --> 00:30:19,130
I don't know.

474
00:30:19,400 --> 00:30:21,282
I guess that depends, Straw Hat.

475
00:30:21,380 --> 00:30:23,400
Maybe I do, and maybe I don't.

476
00:30:24,520 --> 00:30:26,017
What are you talking about?

477
00:30:26,100 --> 00:30:26,982
Did you forget?

478
00:30:27,180 --> 00:30:29,120
No, I didn't forget, you moron!

479
00:30:29,400 --> 00:30:33,257
But I'm not just going to tell you where
he is out of the kindness of my heart.

480
00:30:33,340 --> 00:30:35,164
You have to work for that info.

481
00:30:35,800 --> 00:30:37,580
Fine, I'll make you tell me.

482
00:30:38,900 --> 00:30:42,580
You can give it your best shot,
but I don't like your chances.

483
00:30:43,260 --> 00:30:45,848
I doubt Rubber can
bounce back from a blade.

484
00:30:46,320 --> 00:30:47,220
You're right.

485
00:30:52,080 --> 00:30:53,920
Chop, chop! Ricecracker!

486
00:30:56,400 --> 00:31:00,180
Can't move in mid-air, can you? Too bad.

487
00:31:01,360 --> 00:31:02,680
No, you're wrong!

488
00:31:07,580 --> 00:31:09,440
Oh, how interesting.

489
00:31:11,080 --> 00:31:15,540
You're not so bad either, but
here comes Gum-Gum Hissle!

490
00:31:16,040 --> 00:31:18,040
Their neat abilities, all right,

491
00:31:18,860 --> 00:31:20,566
but they leave you wide open.

492
00:31:21,160 --> 00:31:23,840
I'll carve you up! Gum-Gum!

493
00:31:23,980 --> 00:31:26,660
Jump, jump, quick escape! Hissle!

494
00:31:33,500 --> 00:31:35,400
Not good enough, Gum-Gum.

495
00:31:41,920 --> 00:31:44,540
Damn, you keep breaking into pieces. What?

496
00:31:44,820 --> 00:31:46,349
They're still going at it?

497
00:31:46,820 --> 00:31:48,660
I can't believe these guys.

498
00:31:49,200 --> 00:31:51,580
Uh, hey, did you see that?

499
00:31:51,840 --> 00:31:52,940
You dumbass.

500
00:31:53,080 --> 00:31:54,557
Pretend you're still knocked out.

501
00:31:54,640 --> 00:31:56,917
If you get yourself caught
in the middle of that,

502
00:31:57,000 --> 00:31:59,857
then there's no way you'll
ever make it out alive.

503
00:31:59,940 --> 00:32:01,060
Chop, chop, cannon!

504
00:32:05,160 --> 00:32:05,990
Separate.

505
00:32:10,000 --> 00:32:12,400
So, Rutt, you want to give up yet?

506
00:32:21,340 --> 00:32:23,600
You bastard! How's that?

507
00:32:23,900 --> 00:32:27,018
Was I not supposed to scratch
your face or something?

508
00:32:28,100 --> 00:32:28,930
Bastard!

509
00:32:29,013 --> 00:32:32,440
No one damages my lucky hat
and walks away from it alive!

510
00:32:34,400 --> 00:32:36,357
This hat is my only treasure!

511
00:32:36,440 --> 00:32:40,087
And anyone who so much as lays
a finger on it is going to pay!

512
00:32:41,440 --> 00:32:43,660
Yeah, I made a solemn promise.

513
00:32:43,860 --> 00:32:45,777
I promised the guy who
gave me this hat that I'd

514
00:32:45,860 --> 00:32:48,597
form a crew and become
the greatest pirate ever.

515
00:32:48,680 --> 00:32:52,386
And I didn't think that there
was anything that could faze him.

516
00:32:53,220 --> 00:32:54,600
But look at him.

517
00:32:54,880 --> 00:32:57,300
He's getting so upset about a hat.

518
00:33:01,040 --> 00:33:04,880
Hmm, it seems that hat has a
history to it. That's right!

519
00:33:05,180 --> 00:33:07,240
Is it really all that special?

520
00:33:13,720 --> 00:33:16,960
If that's the case, you should protect it!

521
00:33:33,660 --> 00:33:35,300
I'll leave this hat to you.

522
00:33:35,600 --> 00:33:39,637
It means more to me than anything in the
world, so you better take good care of it.

523
00:33:39,720 --> 00:33:40,550
You hear me?

524
00:33:46,960 --> 00:33:51,640
I want you to bring this hat back
to me someday, in good condition.

525
00:33:52,820 --> 00:33:55,420
And only once you've
become a great pirate.

526
00:33:56,480 --> 00:33:58,080
That's our promise, Luffy.

527
00:34:07,700 --> 00:34:11,347
You really consider this worthless
dirty Straw Hat a treasure?

528
00:34:11,520 --> 00:34:13,140
You need to grow up, boy!

529
00:34:15,120 --> 00:34:16,200
Shut up!

530
00:34:16,960 --> 00:34:19,057
When Shanks gave me
that, I made a promise!

531
00:34:19,140 --> 00:34:19,970
What?

532
00:34:20,053 --> 00:34:23,196
So you're telling me that
this used to be Shanks' hat?

533
00:34:23,540 --> 00:34:25,720
No wonder it looked so familiar.

534
00:34:26,580 --> 00:34:28,840
He always wore it when I knew him.

535
00:34:29,860 --> 00:34:32,957
So you and Shanks were members
of the same pirate crew?

536
00:34:33,040 --> 00:34:33,870
Yeah.

537
00:34:33,953 --> 00:34:38,060
Back when we were pirates in
training, we were fellow comrades.

538
00:34:38,620 --> 00:34:42,200
That damn detestable,
red-haired, Blackford!

539
00:34:43,700 --> 00:34:46,217
Shanks is a much better
man than you'll ever be!

540
00:34:46,300 --> 00:34:51,241
You don't have the right to call him comrade,
and don't you ever badmouth him again!

541
00:34:51,640 --> 00:34:53,699
Time for my chop-chop quick escape!

542
00:34:59,220 --> 00:35:03,396
I don't want you to ever mention
Shakes' name to me again, you bastard!

543
00:35:06,540 --> 00:35:09,364
I can see whatever the
hell I want about Shakes.

544
00:35:12,660 --> 00:35:17,013
Tell me what happened between you and
Shakes and where can I find him now?

545
00:35:17,600 --> 00:35:21,640
Damn it how dare you tear
up my treasured Straw Hat!

546
00:35:23,880 --> 00:35:28,437
Do you really want to
know he's the one person

547
00:35:28,520 --> 00:35:31,817
that I loathe I'll curse
his name for the rest?

548
00:35:31,900 --> 00:35:36,320
of my life, as long as there's
breath in my body, Shanks,

549
00:35:36,700 --> 00:35:39,880
I will never forgive you.

550
00:36:01,900 --> 00:36:05,777
That place before someone could beat me,

551
00:36:05,860 --> 00:36:09,977
the promised land was in my grasp

552
00:36:10,060 --> 00:36:11,937
and I wouldn't let

553
00:36:12,020 --> 00:36:17,917
Go my only dream,

554
00:36:18,000 --> 00:36:23,057
I won't stop chasing

555
00:36:23,140 --> 00:36:25,740
it until it comes true

556
00:36:27,420 --> 00:36:31,217
But if the world ever changes,

557
00:36:31,300 --> 00:36:37,197
I call out your name We could return

558
00:36:37,280 --> 00:36:40,960
to the time when everything's the same

559
00:36:41,700 --> 00:36:48,040
As long as I'm with you,
my memories won't fade

560
00:36:48,760 --> 00:36:53,277
Waiting for that one true dream?

561
00:36:53,360 --> 00:36:54,980
We'll be back.
